{"name":"The Blues Brothers","hex":"#214daa","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blues","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of blue"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A feeling of sadness or depression.","One's particular life experience, particularly including the hardships one has faced."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blues"},{"term":"brothers","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of brother"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of brother"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brothers"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Blues Brothers","blocks":[{"text":"The Blues Brothers are an American blues and soul revue band founded in 1978 by comedians Dan Aykroyd and John Belushi, who met and began collaborating as original cast members of Saturday Night Live. The band was primarily a blues, rhythm and blues, and soul music band, with influences from other classic American genres such as jump blues, country music, jazz, and rock and roll."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f5/BluesBrothers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Blues_Brothers","wikidata":"Q1344949"},{"title":"The Blues Brothers (film)","blocks":[{"text":"The Blues Brothers is a 1980 American musical action comedy film directed by John Landis. It stars John Belushi as \"Joliet\" Jake Blues and Dan Aykroyd as his brother Elwood, characters developed from the recurring musical sketch \"The Blues Brothers\" on NBC's variety series Saturday Night Live. The script is set in and around Chicago, Illinois, where it was filmed, and the screenplay is by Aykroyd and Landis. It features musical numbers by singers James Brown, Cab Calloway, Aretha Franklin, Ray Charles and John Lee Hooker. It features non-musical supporting performances by Carrie Fisher and Henry Gibson."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ae/Bluesbrothersmovieposter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Blues_Brothers_(film)","wikidata":"Q109767"},{"title":"Blues","blocks":[{"text":"Blues is a music genre and musical form that originated among African Americans in the Deep South of the United States around the 1860s. Blues has incorporated spirituals, work songs, field hollers, shouts, chants, and rhymed simple narrative ballads from the African-American culture. The blues form is ubiquitous in jazz, rhythm and blues, and rock and roll, and is characterized by the call-and-response pattern, the blues scale, and specific chord progressions, of which the twelve-bar blues is the most common. Blue notes, usually thirds, fifths or sevenths flattened in pitch, are also an essential part of the sound. Blues shuffles or walking bass reinforce the trance-like rhythm and form a repetitive effect known as the groove."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blues","wikidata":"Q9759"},{"title":"Brother","blocks":[{"text":"A brother is a man or boy who shares one or more parents with another; a male sibling. The female counterpart is a sister. Although the term typically refers to a familial relationship, it is sometimes used endearingly to refer to non-familial relationships. A full brother is a first degree relative."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Jackson_5_1969.jpg/330px-Jackson_5_1969.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brother","wikidata":"Q10861465"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/NROL-7_Mission_Patch.png/500px-NROL-7_Mission_Patch.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/NROL-7_Mission_Patch.png/500px-NROL-7_Mission_Patch.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Blues Brothers featured on the National Reconnaissance Office launch number 7 (NROL-7) mission patch","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANROL-7_Mission_Patch.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/f4/Blues_Brothers_car_chase.JPG/330px-Blues_Brothers_car_chase.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/f4/Blues_Brothers_car_chase.JPG/330px-Blues_Brothers_car_chase.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Bluesmobile races through the mall while being chased by state troopers in a scene of the film.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlues_Brothers_car_chase.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Daley_Plaza_060716.jpg/500px-Daley_Plaza_060716.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Daley_Plaza_060716.jpg/500px-Daley_Plaza_060716.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Richard J. Daley Center is Chicago's premier civic center and features a massive sculpture by Pablo Picasso.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADaley_Plaza_060716.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Rusty-s_TV_and_Movie_Car_Museum_Jackson_TN_018.jpg/500px-Rusty-s_TV_and_Movie_Car_Museum_Jackson_TN_018.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Rusty-s_TV_and_Movie_Car_Museum_Jackson_TN_018.jpg/500px-Rusty-s_TV_and_Movie_Car_Museum_Jackson_TN_018.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Reproduction of the \"Bluesmobile\" at Rusty's TV & Movie Car Museum, Jackson, Tennessee","link":"https://e